From e0280e28494200498f6969e74cc9e1681a1d5e4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Zim <235131889+zimcontent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:16:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(runner): a press that opens a window hears of its
 release

A click on something that calls window.open (a "Continue with Google"
button) answered "CDP command timed out: Input.dispatchMouseEvent" 30 s
later, though it had landed. The runner's traffic counter asked for
Target.setAutoAttach at the browser's level, and while any client does
so Chrome never acknowledges the release of a press that opens a window.

The counter now asks to be told of targets (Target.setDiscoverTargets)
and attaches to each page, extension page, service worker and shared
worker itself (Target.attachToTarget, flat). Frames and dedicated
workers are still auto-attached under their page, which holds nothing.
What each session gets is unchanged, the password guard included.

The same click now takes 0.8 s. ADR 0040 section 20.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
